    <p class="lead">Perplexity conversations often mix answers, sources, and follow-ups. That’s valuable research history — and it’s fragile if it only lives in the web app.</p>
    <h2>When to backup</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Before switching plans or accounts</li>
      <li>After a deep research sprint you may cite later</li>
      <li>If you use Perplexity alongside ChatGPT/Claude and want one archive location</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Backup with TotalRecalls</h2>
    <p>TotalRecalls treats Perplexity as a first-class provider on Windows:</p>
